      "document_id": "DOC001",
      "content": "The UAP has nothing to do with government expenditure. Fiscal policy only affects exchange rates if it influences interest rates. Expansionary fiscal policy can lead to a larger output gap, prompting the Fed to raise interest rates. When the Fed raises interest rates, the domestic currency tends to appreciate. Investors expect the Fed to react to expansionary fiscal policy by raising rates.",
